<p>A few names are aliases that resolve to the same code: <code>GREEN</code> and
  <code>LIGHT_GREEN</code>, <code>PURPLE</code> and <code>DARK_MAGENTA</code>, <code>ORANGE</code> and
  <code>LIGHT_ORANGE</code>. Note also that the orange family sits on the terminal's yellow and red
  slots rather than on a true orange, which is the main reason those three render differently from one
  terminal to the next. Where an exact shade matters, reach for the brown ramp instead.</p>

<p><code>DEFAULT</code> emits no code at all, leaving the text in the terminal's own foreground color.
  That is the value both <code>color</code> and <code>bg_color</code> take when you pass neither.</p>

